Weather API Dashboard

Overview
The Weather API Dashboard is a simple web application that demonstrates how REST APIs work in a real-world frontend project.
It allows users to:
Fetch live weather data using a city name (GET request)
Save new locations (POST request)
Modify saved locations (PUT request)
Remove locations (DELETE request)

This project helps in understanding how frontend applications communicate with external APIs.

Features
Search weather by city name
Display temperature, humidity, wind speed, and weather conditions
Save favorite locations (POST)
Edit saved locations (PUT)
Delete saved locations (DELETE)
View API response data in real-time
Technologies Used
HTML5 – Structure of the application
CSS3 – Styling and layout
JavaScript (Vanilla JS) – Logic and API handling
OpenWeatherMap API – Weather data source
JSONPlaceholder API – Mock API for CRUD operations

How to Run the Project
Download or clone the repository
Open the project folder in VS Code
Open index.html in your browser
Enter a city name and click Get Weather
Test other operations using the available tabs
API Endpoints Used
Weather API (GET)
https://api.openweathermap.org/data/2.5/weather
Create Location (POST)
https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts
Update Location (PUT)
https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/{id}
Delete Location (DELETE)
https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/{id}

What I Learned
Through this project, I learned:

How REST APIs work in frontend applications
How to use different HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
How to fetch and display API data using JavaScript
How frontend and backend systems communicate